 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Agent form tools
+
+The sign-in and sign-up pages expose `sign_in` and `sign_up` respectively
+through the [WebMCP declarative form API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api).
+Both tools accept required `username` and `password` strings and automatically
+submit through the same client-side handlers used by people. Tools are available
+while their form is on the page, in browsers with declarative WebMCP enabled.
+
+Agent submissions receive `{ success: boolean, message: string }` after the
+request finishes, including API and network failures. Credentials and API tokens
+are not included in tool results. In browsers without WebMCP, the forms continue
+to work normally.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
